<title>UK: Exco H1 pre-tax profit drops to 12.1 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Exco H1 pre-tax profit drops to 12.1 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>			  (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		  5.1		  vs 7.0</p>
<p> Dividend  (pence)	  1.5		  vs 3.0</p>
<p> Pretax profit		12.1		 vs 16.1</p>
<p> Turnover		     113.7		vs 109.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Wholesale securities broker Exco Plc said its revenue had been hit by a decline in volumes and pressure on commission rates, adding that its markets remained disappointing.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 11.04		  vs 14.35</p>
<p> Interest receivable    1.56		   vs 1.66</p>
<p> Interest payable	 0.90		   vs 0.62</p>
<p> Tax			  5.58		   vs 6.93</p>
<p> Net taxed		  6.55		   vs 9.13</p>
<p> Attributable	     6.33		   vs 8.60</p>
<p> Pay date		   October 30</p>
<p> Div registration date  October 22</p>
<p> Ex-div date		October 14</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
